    "wf_questions": {
      "type": "wave-fy27-questions",
      "blocks": {
        "question_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Running costs",
            "question": "How much does it cost to run?",
            "answer": "<p>It depends on how often you use it and what you pay for electricity. The calculator above works it out for this spa: pick a size, how often you'll soak and your unit rate. Keep the cover on between soaks, and add the EnergySave™ bundle to bring it down further.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Space",
            "question": "Will it fit in my garden?",
            "answer": "<p>Check the footprint in the size options and leave around a metre clear around it, for getting in and out and reaching the filter. It needs somewhere flat, firm and level. Filled with water and people, a spa can weigh a tonne or more, so decking must be rated for that load.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Power",
            "question": "What power do I need?",
            "answer": "<p>A standard 13 amp outdoor socket with RCD protection. There's no hard-wiring and no electrician to book. Plug it straight into the socket rather than using an extension lead.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Looking after it",
            "question": "How much looking after does it need?",
            "answer": "<p>A few minutes a week. Rinse the filter after a soak and test the water twice a week (chlorine 3 to 5 ppm, pH 7.2 to 7.6). Give the filter a deeper clean weekly, fit a new cartridge every 2 to 4 weeks and refresh the water every 1 to 3 months.</p><p>Our water care guides take you through it step by step.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "All year",
            "question": "Can I use it in winter?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. It heats to 40°C all year round. Keep the cover on between soaks to hold the heat. On models with automatic frost protection, it switches on by itself when the temperature drops below 5°C.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Noise",
            "question": "Is it noisy?",
            "answer": "<p>The heater and filter pump make a low hum. The bubbles are the loudest part, and on two-speed models the lower setting is noticeably quieter, which suits late evenings and close neighbours.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Planning",
            "question": "Do I need planning permission?",
            "answer": "<p>In most UK gardens, no: a hot tub usually counts as permitted development. Check with your local council if you live in a listed building, a conservation area or a flat, or if you're building decking more than 30cm off the ground.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Delivery",
            "question": "When will it arrive?",
            "answer": "<p>Order by 6:30pm for free next-day tracked delivery with DPD, who'll send you a one-hour delivery window. Saturday delivery is available for £9.99.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Warranty",
            "question": "What's the warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>Every spa comes with a 2-year warranty, backed by our UK support team: Monday to Friday 8:30 to 5:30, and Saturday 8 to 4. We reply to emails within 8 working hours.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "topic": "Paying",
            "question": "Can I spread the cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Pay in 3 with Klarna, or spread it monthly and interest-free with DivideBuy, subject to eligibility. You'll find the options just under the price.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "question_1",
        "question_2",
        "question_3",
        "question_4",
        "question_5",
        "question_6",
        "question_7",
        "question_8",
